From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suvojeet-sengupta <suvojitsengupta21@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:06:02 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: Don't let apps read the keystore compat props

Every app could read sys.keystore_compat.active and
sys.tee_simulator.active. Banking and payment apps can list the
properties they can read, and these names say outright that key
attestation is being faked, which fits GPay and PhonePe refusing to
work on AOSPA with strong integrity while PenguinOS, which doesn't
have them, works. Only GMS and the Play Store, where PIHooks checks
them, need them.
---
 sepolicy/private/appdomain.te | 5 +++--
 sepolicy/private/priv_app.te  | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 sepolicy/private/priv_app.te

diff --git a/sepolicy/private/appdomain.te b/sepolicy/private/appdomain.te
index 40ef5f4..6a84724 100644
--- a/sepolicy/private/appdomain.te
+++ b/sepolicy/private/appdomain.te
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 get_prop(appdomain, pih_disable_prop)
 
-# Keystore compatibility
-get_prop(appdomain, keystore_compat_prop)
+# Keystore compatibility. Root and spoofing checks in apps list every
+# property they can read, so only GMS and the Play Store get to read it
+dontaudit appdomain keystore_compat_prop:file { getattr map open read };
diff --git a/sepolicy/private/priv_app.te b/sepolicy/private/priv_app.te
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..16dec6c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sepolicy/private/priv_app.te
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+# Keystore compatibility, for the Play Store's key attestation check
+get_prop(priv_app, keystore_compat_prop)
-- 
2.55.0

